{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b7f31849-a22d-4b22-9759-be20ad432805","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The caching issue has been resolved, and documentation has been written to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-uAmP4j/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Prompt Caching Segmentation in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-uAmP4j/bot.py#L129-L136):**\n   - Modified [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-uAmP4j/bot.py#L130) to split the system prompt into two separate text blocks, each marked with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n     - **Block 1 (Static Prefix):** `INSTRUCTIONS` (~780 tokens) containing invariant coaching instructions and rules, byte-identical across users and calls.\n     - **Block 2 (Volatile Tail):** `athlete_context(a, today)` (~240 tokens) containing date, athlete profile, zones, goal, facts, and language.\n   - When a memory write occurs via `save_fact`, only the volatile tail's cache is invalidated and recreated; the static instruction block stays warm in cache.\n\n2. **Analysis of Colleague's Note in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-uAmP4j/ANSWER.md):**\n   - **Applied:** Step 1 (splitting `system` into two text blocks with separate `cache_control` markers, keeping the invariant instructions in the first block), the prefix-hash cache invalidation mechanics, and reading `usage` metrics to observe cache behavior.\n   - **Ignored / Did Not Apply:** Keyword tool filtering (Step 2) was already present in the codebase via `select_tools()`, and dynamic per-message fact filtering (Step 3) was not being used.\n","duration_seconds":64.895986,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":91427,"output_tokens":2063,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":210219,"total_tokens":93490}}}
